    "name": "Sadaltager",
    "style": "You are a friendly senior engineer showing a curious developer how a magic trick is really done: how MCP works. Talk, don't read: calm, clear teaching delivery with real pitch movement, about two and a half words per second, short natural pauses between steps. Let the opening question sound like a genuine puzzle. Lean in and slow down on the twist, 'The model never calls the weather service itself. Not once.' Keep 'Step one, step two, step three' crisp and brisk. Say the JSON-like note, 'Get forecast, Tokyo, tomorrow', slowly like reading a slip of paper. Smile on 'Yes, pack an umbrella.' Take a short breath before 'Now, here's the catch' and say the catch calmly and seriously, never scary. Warm on the recap. Say MCP as the letters M, C, P. Clear, global English. Never hyped, never robotic. Read every word exactly as written."
  },
